  "narrative": "Wellington R1037 of 12 Operational Training Unit took off from Chipping Warden on a night training flight on 20 October 1941. It crashed in Chipping Warden village at about 23:10 while attempting to go round again, and caught fire. Pilot Officer Kenneth Farnes was killed. Pilot Officer Cecil Harry Hayes was seriously injured and died of his injuries on 21 October. Farnes was 30 and is buried at Brookwood Military Cemetery; Hayes is buried in Malden churchyard.",
